# Snapshot CONTENT stays local. The live ~/.claude tree can drift to include
# material that has no business in a git history, and history is exactly where a
# later delete does not remove it. So the bytes live only on this machine.
#
# The MANIFEST is tracked on purpose: paths, sizes and sha256 are what prove the
# shape of the tree at a moment without carrying the tree, and `snap.py diff`
# needs only the manifest, so drift detection survives a fresh clone.
*/files/
